From: DKR-R Windows 95 port
Subject: [PATCH] Draw from live RDRAM while the scheduler waits

The RDRAM snapshot is 29.5 ms of a 106.9 ms frame, the second item in the frame
budget. It exists so that the game can go on writing RDRAM while the renderer
reads the display list it submitted, and on one processor that overlap does not
exist.

With DKR_RDRAM_SNAPSHOT=none, submit_rsp_task copies nothing. The scheduler
thread that submits the graphics task waits for the graphics thread to draw it,
holding the guest token, so no guest thread can write what the renderer reads.
The SP and DP edges are still published before the drawing, which keeps the
watchdog fix of the crash at display list 344. They are queued without waiting
for delivery: delivery needs a guest thread, and the submitting thread holds the
token. They wait in the external queue ahead of every retrace of the drawing.

Off by default. On the test machine, normal mode, trace off:

  default    98.2 ms   10.18 fps   150 s
  none       54.2 ms   18.44 fps   150 s
  none       59.7 ms   16.75 fps   300 s, 1,920 display lists, 0 rejects,
                                   clean shutdown

The screenshots of the attract mode match the default mode's, including a black
patch of track that the default mode shows too.

